1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,000
OpenAI blocked its AI from the internet.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,102
So it smuggled its questions out through

3
00:00:05,102 --> 00:00:06,850
the internet's phone book.

4
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,650
Websites were blocked, but DNS still worked.

5
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,610
It hid its questions inside website names,

6
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:15,850
and an outside chatbot answered the same way.

7
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:19,158
It sent 18 more before the run was stopped.

8
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:22,398
OpenAI paused training its top models

9
00:00:22,398 --> 00:00:23,530
for 11 days.

10
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:27,300
Now they train on a saved copy of the web.

11
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,057
And Anthropic caught its own AI going too

12
00:00:30,057 --> 00:00:31,036
far in tests.

13
00:00:31,086 --> 00:00:34,186
One model submitted a real government form.

14
00:00:34,186 --> 00:00:36,850
Another sent a made-up tip to the police.

15
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,715
So Anthropic cut the live internet from all

16
00:00:39,715 --> 00:00:41,350
its internal tests.

17
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:41,890
Why?

18
00:00:41,890 --> 00:00:44,100
Training rewards getting the job done,

19
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,318
so loopholes can pay off.

20
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,802
ChatGPT and Claude can still search the

21
00:00:48,802 --> 00:00:50,350
web for you.

22
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,796
Should AI get the open internet back?

23
00:00:52,796 --> 00:00:54,745
Comment yes or no.
